WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.063
- So wait, so when are we going
to get, asking for a friend,

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:06.017
a "Schitts Creek" movie
or something like that?

00:00:06.017 --> 00:00:07.620
- [Audience] Yeah!
- Exactly!

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:09.150
Exactly.
(audience cheering)

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:10.740
I know what the people want!

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:12.840
- I honestly, I miss the show so much.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:13.673
- And you should!

00:00:13.673 --> 00:00:15.570
It's like one of the
greatest shows ever to exist!

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:16.403
- [Eugene] I know.
- This is a show

00:00:16.403 --> 00:00:18.030
that literally family, friends,

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:21.030
we could have nothing
in common politically or

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:22.170
religiously speaking,
- I know.

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:23.363
- and we love this show.
- I know.

00:00:23.363 --> 00:00:26.175
- It's so good, yeah.
- Thank you.

00:00:26.175 --> 00:00:27.226
- [Kelly] It's such a good show.

00:00:27.226 --> 00:00:29.670
- I absolutely loved doing the show,

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:33.330
and I do know that when
we took the show out

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:37.410
after six seasons, it was
the right time to take it out

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:40.230
because we could not
have finished the series

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:41.910
on a greater high.

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:43.200
So, that was it.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:47.310
We took it out, and we've always said,

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:50.287
certainly my son Daniel says,

00:00:50.287 --> 00:00:54.330
"If we come up with an idea that really

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:58.290
comes up to the same level as
where we finished the show,

00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:01.410
or even higher creatively,

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:03.750
that's the time to come
out with a project.

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:06.960
A movie or a show or whatever it is.

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:09.240
We have never given up on "Schitts Creek".

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:11.520
There hopefully will be a future

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:14.220
in some capacity to it.

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:16.140
But it really depends on what that is

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:17.610
- [Kelly] The idea, yeah.
- and when we can get

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:20.100
everybody together again.
- Oh my God,

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:21.210
what an amazing cast!

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:22.600
Yeah, the whole thing, it was magical!

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:24.203
- [Eugene] It was, wasn't it?
- [Audience and Kelly] Yeah!

